<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70522" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεῦσις</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inclination, tendency</i> of
			physical forces to or from a centre, <i><span class="en">
				Ti.Locr.
				100d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεύσεις, αἱ,</span> title of work by Apollonius of Perga, problems
			where a straight line has to be drawn through a point so as to
			intercept a given length between two lines or curves, <i><span class="en">
				Papp.
				670.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>downward tendency, gravitation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1122c
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				1.131
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>tendency, inclination,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				1.1.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> in
			Neo-Platonic philosophy, <i>declension</i> in the scale of Being,
			esp. of the Soul, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἡ πρὸς σῶμα καὶ ὕλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.6.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. εἰς</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν γένεσιν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>in CA</u>
				26p.479M.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Antr.</u>
				11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πρὸς τὸ χεῖρον ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					5.166d
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
